--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lazy-wave power cable with discrete buoyancy modules and a bend stiffener on a moving vessel in a current, 36 s
-- The 80 m Gulf of Mexico cable of lazy_wave_buoyancy_modules.dat: its buoyant stretch is ten
-- discrete modules (ATTACHMENTS series 70.614:5.0:115.614) on the bare cable, in a 0.3 m/s
-- current along -X, from the touchdown toward the hang-off; seabed friction (0.5) holds the
-- grounded tail. The hang-off carries the 4 m polyurethane bend stiffener of
-- lazy_wave_bend_stiffener.dat (STIFFENERS: a 0.4 m cylindrical root and a 3.6 m cone) and is
-- clamped (Rigid) along its static tangent on the vessel of lazy_wave_vessel_motion.dat
-- (vesselMotion: 1.5 m surge, 2 m heave and 3 deg pitch at 12 s, after a 12 s smooth start).
-- The mesh puts 0.15 m elements under the stiffener and a couple of metres past its tip, and a
-- node at every module, 0.5 m apart along the buoyant stretch. The modules and the stiffener
-- both enter the static solve, so the march starts in the equilibrium in the current.
-- BendMom1N1 + StfMom1N1 is the root moment, BendMom1N1 the cable's share; Curv1N28 samples
-- the cable 4.05 m from the root, just past the stiffener tip. The Outputs flag r writes the
-- range graph (tension, curvature, bend moment, declination and seabed clearance envelopes
-- from RangeStart) to <root>.Line1.range.out.
